courses.learning_outcomes:
• be aware of the safety of the selected racquet sports,

• demonstrate basic skills and knowledge on the rules and regulations of the selected racquet sports;
• demonstrate appropriate teaching strategies in teaching and/or coaching racquet sports;
• design innovative training strategies for teaching and/or coaching racquet sports; and

• develop the missions to promote racquet sports to different target groups in a professional manner.

• perform basic skills in tennis;
• demonstrate knowledge of the theoretical aspect;
• apply the skills and tactics in single and double plays (real game situations);
• demonstrate ability in skill analysis;
• acquire and demonstrate teaching skills; and

• advocate the values and standards of the teaching and coaching profession.

• be aware of the safety of the games;
• demonstrate the knowledge of basic skills, tactics, rules and regulations;
• present appropriate teaching strategies; and
• perform the basic skills of squash.

• Perform the basic skills of Butterfly and Backstroke;
• Demonstrate advanced swimming skills (tumble turn and diving start)
• Demonstrate teaching of Butterfly and Backstroke;
• Understand the theoretical aspect of Butterfly and Backstroke;
• Demonstrate the ability of specific Butterfly and Backstroke skill analysis;
• Plan and implement appropriate classes for Butterfly and Backstroke.

• Perform the basic skills of Track Events;
• Demonstrate the teaching skills of Track Events;
• Demonstrate the theoretical aspect of Track Events;
• Demonstrate the ability of Track Events skill analysis;
• Plan and implement appropriate classes of Track Events.

• Perform the basic skills of Field Events;
• Demonstrate the teaching skills of Field Events;
• Demonstrate the theoretical aspect of Field Events;
• Demonstrate the ability of Field Events skill analysis;
• Plan and implement appropriate classes of Field Events.

• identify 5 major components of rope skipping;
• identify different forms of skipping in 5 major components;
• perform different skills in single rope, partner rope, traveller, long rope and double dutch;
• write lesson plans in teaching rope skipping;
• apply the knowledge in rope skipping in curriculum planning.

courses.course_syllabus:
• Use of cone, sash, rings and other equipment to enhance teaching rope skipping;
• Relationships between rope skipping and fitness;
• Different forms of single rope skills;
• Different forms of partner rope skills;
• Different forms of traveller skills

• Different forms of long rope skills

• Different forms of double dutch skills

• Inclusion of rope skipping in P.E. curriculum;
• Lessons planning in rope skipping unit.

